  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "9eXWGZSkUsIquYDE9C+w9NV+Qkw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:44.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "**Decision (aligned, Aug 12 meeting):** the project adopts a strategy to prioritize existing software solutions over custom development to avoid unnecessary reinvention of the wheel.\n\nConcretely, evaluation precedes building (02:12:24\u201302:15:06):\n- **Plannerly** \u2014 documentation and templates for the PM-level BIM documents (EIR, BEP); machine-readable documents supporting automated BIM checks\n- **BIMQ Neo** \u2014 manages project phases, BIM use cases, and information requirements\n- **Build BIM Permit** \u2014 checks models against building regulations based on Information Delivery Specifications (IDS)\n\nWouter framed the principle: identify concrete use cases and verify whether existing tools solve them before developing new solutions. The complementary revenue logic from the Aug 14 weekly: leveraging mature external software (like Speckle) lets the team offer high-value consultancy in the short term while the scalable product develops (00:35:41).\n\nFollow-ups assigned: Agli Hysi to evaluate Plannerly, share BIM property lists, retrospectives and lessons learned; Wouter to review BIMQ Neo.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T18:11:44.616305+00:00"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:44.000Z"
    }
  },
